# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DevHub API — build context filter for `docker build -t devhub-api:local api`
#
# Everything listed here is invisible to the daemon. Two reasons that matter:
#   1. Speed — the context is uploaded on every build, and bin/obj dwarf the source.
#   2. Correctness — a host bin/ copied into the image would shadow the artifacts
#      `dotnet publish` produces inside the container, so "works locally" would
#      quietly mean "built on my machine, with my SDK".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Build output -----------------------------------------------------------
# **/ matters: a bare `bin/` only matches the context root, not src/*/bin.
**/bin/
**/obj/

# --- Tests and the solution that owns them ----------------------------------
# These travel as a pair on purpose. The image is a runtime artifact, so the test
# project has no business in it — and once tests/ is excluded, DevHub.sln points at
# projects that no longer exist in the context. That is why the build restores
# src/DevHub.Api/DevHub.Api.csproj and never the solution (see Dockerfile).
tests/
DevHub.sln

# --- Developer-machine configuration ----------------------------------------
# launchSettings.json is IDE/`dotnet run` configuration, not application settings.
# The container gets its configuration from environment variables at runtime.
Properties/launchSettings.json
appsettings.Local.json
*.user

# --- Never, under any circumstances ------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
secrets.json

# --- Noise -------------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.vs/
.idea/
*.swp
**/*.http
